## DESCRIPTION
## Calculus
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## Tagged by tda2d

## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Applications of differentiation)
## DBsection(Global extrema)
## Date(8/23/07)
## Institution(Rochester)
## Level(4)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('Calculus: Early Transcendentals')
## AuthorText1('Rogawski')
## EditionText1('1')
## Section1('4.2')
## Problem1('41')
## KEYWORDS('derivative' 'extrema' 'optimization','Optimization', 'Absolute', 'Extrema')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

$a  = random(3, 9, 3);
$a1 = $a * 2 / 3;
$a2 = $a / 3;
$a3 = $a2**3;

$f = Formula("$a (x^2)^(1/3)-2x");

# interval
$c0 = random(-9, -5);
$c1 = $a3;

# x value at the maximum.
$xval = ($f->eval(x => $c0) > $f->eval(x => $c1)) ? $c0 : $c1;

BEGIN_PGML
Determine where the absolute extrema of [`` f(x)=[$a] x^{2/3} - 2x  ``] on the interval [` [[$c0],[$c1]] `] occur.

a) The absolute maximum occurs at [`x=`] [_]{$xval}

b) The absolute minimum occurs at [`x=`] [_]{Real(0)}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_HINT
Extreme values can occur at singular points (when [`f'(x)`] is undefined).
END_PGML_HINT

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Since the function [`` f(x)=[$a] x^{2/3} - 2x  ``] is defined at every [`x`] on [`[[$c0], [$c1]]`], we simply take derivative of the function to find the critical points, we obtain:
[```f'(x) = [$a]\cdot \frac{2}{3} x^{-1/3} - 2 = \frac{[$a1]}{x^{1/3}} - 2```]
Setting this to zero and solve for [`x`]
[``` x^{1/3} = \frac{6}{2} \qquad \Longrightarrow \qquad x = ([$a2])^3 = [$a3] ```]

Since the function [`f'(x)`] is not defined at [`x = 0`], the critical points will be  [`x = 0`], and [`x = [$a3]`].  We also evaluate this at the right endpoint of the interval or [`x= [$c0]`]. 

 Substitute all of these into [`f(x)`] we get
[```
\begin{aligned}
f([$c0]) & = [$f->eval(x => $c0)]\\
f(0) &  = 0 \\
f([$a3]) & = [$f->eval(x => $a3)]\\
\end{aligned}
```]

Therefore, the maximum of the function [`f(x)`] is at [`x = [$xval] `] and the minimum of the function [`f(x)`] is at [`x = 0`].
END_PGML_SOLUTION

ENDDOCUMENT();
